      "problem": "Find the first four non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\frac{1}{1+ax}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-ax$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+ax} & =1+(-ax)+(-ax)^{2}+(-ax)^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+(-1)ax+(-1)^{2}{a}^{2}{x}^{2}+(-1)^{3}{a}^{3}{x}^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-ax+{a}^{2}{x}^{2}-{a}^{3}{x}^{3}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
